  "history_summaries": [
    "Round 1/3: Fixed DUT counter saturation bug. Error type: dut_bug. Assertion handled: usb_rst_requires_max_cnt (and also se0_eventually_triggers_usb_reset and non_se0_clears_counter indirectly). Root cause: rst_cnt had no terminal-count guard in the increment path, causing it to wrap past 31 in the same cycle usb_rst_reg became active, violating !usb_rst_reg || rst_cnt===31. Fix: added && rst_cnt < 31.U to the increment condition on line 78 (now line 78), preventing wrap-around and ensuring rst_cnt saturates at 31. Causal reasoning: the counter increment condition !usb_rst_reg && fs_ce did not gate on terminal count, so rst_cnt could exit 31 in the same clock cycle usb_rst_reg sampled the (rst_cnt===31) comparison, causing a one-cycle skew between register assertion and counter value. The fix stops counting at 31 so both signals remain consistent. All assertions preserved (not deleted/renamed/weakened). No homologous assertions found."
